# Assembly limits recount the full pre-optimization baseline (f4306dc), including code after numeric trap labels.
# the counts the passes reach; a pass lowers these, nothing raises them without saying so.
# The float blend, the wrapping add, the shift, the bit operations and the broadcasts are one
# vector instruction each; the checked multiply and the folds still read the lanes.
# 0.7.0: the optimiser (single-assignment form, value numbering, load elimination) lowered
# every count it could; the vectors' folds and checked multiply still read the lanes.
# 0.11.0: the register allocator over the exact lives, with the caller-saved registers for
# the temporaries that cross no call, lowered the assembly count.
# 0.15.0: x12 and x13 joined the caller-saved pool on arm64; the counts lowered to what the
# passes reach today.
# 0.17.2: the argument registers x0–x7 joined that pool, a call filling them by a parallel
# move; the generators read operands and addresses where they live.
# 0.17.4: r8, r9, rsi and rdi joined the x86-64 SysV pool the same way; the x86-64 counts
# lowered to what the passes reach.
ir 310
loads 39
stores 46
calls 11
asm-arm64 464
asm-x86_64 639
